/**
\page response_formalism Response formalism — the equations the code implements

This page fixes the symbols used in the Doxygen of molresponse and indexes the equations,
each of which is stated at the object that implements it. Everything follows from the
time-dependent Hartree--Fock / Kohn--Sham orbital equation expanded order by order in the
field, with orthonormality of the occupied orbitals (the orbital form of density-matrix
idempotency) imposed at each order. The equations are those of the release report
2026-09-09 (`madness-workspace/reports/2026-09-09_release_report/main.tex`, §1 "Formalism");
the derivations are in `madness-workspace/reports/2026-09-08_first_principles_derivation` and
`madness-workspace/reports/2026-09-09_orientation_derivation`. `madness-workspace`
(`github.com/ahurta92/madness-workspace`) is the companion repository these reports live in.

\section rf_conventions Objects and conventions

Occupied orbitals \f$\phi_i\f$ (\f$i=1..N_{\rm occ}\f$, closed shell), ground-state Fock
operator \f$F^{0}\f$ with \f$F^{0}\phi_i=\epsilon_i\phi_i\f$, projector onto the virtual space
\f$\hat Q=1-\sum_i|\phi_i\rangle\langle\phi_i|\f$. A pair density \f$\gamma(r,r')\f$ has the
diagonal \f$\rho_\gamma(r)=\gamma(r,r)\f$ (carrying the closed-shell factor 2) and enters through
the first derivative of the two-electron operator \f$g'[\gamma]\f$ (\ref rr_eq_gprime "(g')"), with
\f$c_x=1\f$ for Hartree--Fock (the DFT kernel adds \f$f_{\rm xc}[\rho_\gamma]\f$ and, at second
order, a \f$g''\f$ term that vanishes for HF).

Every convention that matters is fixed by one statement: <em>a response density at
\f$+\omega\f$ is \f$\gamma^{B}=|x^{B}\rangle\langle\phi|+|\phi\rangle\langle y^{B}|\f$, and its
dagger is the same density at \f$-\omega\f$</em> (\ref rr_eq_legs "(legs)"). In the code this is spelled
out by source_spec::gamma_legs, source_spec::gamma_dagger_legs and source_spec::ketbra; every
second-order term is written with them.

\section rf_index Correspondence with the code

| equation | object | code | gate |
|---|---|---|---|
| \ref rr_eq_lin "(lin)", \ref rr_eq_bsh "(bsh)", \ref rr_eq_alpha "(alpha)" | FD solve, protocol ladder | calc_executor.hpp: solve_fd_protocol | — |
| (lin) with \f$v=0\f$, \ref rr_eq_esnorm "(esnorm)" | ES eigenproblem (TDA / Full) | es_solver.hpp: ESSolver | — |
| \ref rr_eq_gprime "(g')", \ref rr_eq_legs "(legs)" | kernel and legs | two_electron.hpp: apply_gamma_raw; source_spec.hpp: gamma_legs | — |
| \ref rr_eq_gammaL "(gammaL)", \ref rr_eq_PQ "(PQ)" | the one source | tpa_source_spec.hpp: quadratic_source; vbc.hpp: compute_vbc_spec | tests/test_vbc_spec_equivalence, tests/test_tpa_pq_vs_vbc |
| \ref rr_eq_beta "(beta)" | \f$2n{+}1\f$ contraction | beta.hpp: beta_abc | — |
| \ref rr_eq_raman "(raman)" | nuclear leg | Perturbations.hpp: nuclear_operator | — |
| \ref rr_eq_spec "(spec)", \ref rr_eq_tpa "(tpa)" | 2PA moments | tpa.hpp: tpa_moment_residue_1e + tpa_pq_spec_sym (default); tpa_sources, tpa_moment_residue (legacy vbc path) | — |

\section rf_reading How to read a second-order term

\f$\beta\f$ contracts \f$(P,Q)\f$ (\ref rr_eq_PQ "(PQ)") with a driven leg at \f$+\omega_\sigma\f$ and adds
the unrelaxed trace \f$\mathrm{Tr}(v^{A}\gamma_L^{BC})\f$; Raman is the same contraction with the
\f$C\f$ leg the static response to \f$v^{Q}\f$; 2PA contracts the same \f$(P,Q)\f$ with an
eigenvector and drops the trace. The residue introduces no dagger and changes nothing inside
\f$(P,Q)\f$.

\par See also
`docs/guides/formalism.md` (the same equations, prose form, GitHub-rendered) and `README.md`
(where this page sits among the other molresponse documentation).
*/
